## How to read this

Use the exact section order below: `P1`, `P2`, `P3`, `P?`, `Done`.

Every active item must use one of these forms:

- In `P1` / `P2` / `P3`: `- [ ] **[M] Title** — description` where the effort
  is one of `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`
- In `## P?`: `- [ ] **[?/L] Title** — description` where the effort is one of
  `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`

A trailing `→ [research](backlog/<slug>.md)` link means the item has
accompanying investigation, design notes, or paused troubleshooting.

When implementing an item, move it to `## Done` in the same commit using:

- `- ✅ [YYYY-MM-DD] [P#/Effort] Title — one-line shipped summary`

---

## P1

- [ ] **[S] Example small item** — short description with file paths if helpful.

## P2

- [ ] **[M] Example medium item** — link to research if non-trivial. → [research](backlog/example-medium.md)

## P3

- [ ] **[S] Example deferred item** — low signal-to-effort, but easy.

## P?

- [ ] **[?/L] Example evaluation item** — what spike would answer the question? → [research](backlog/example-evaluation.md)

